# Line endings and binary files.
#
# Goal: a fresh clone is byte-identical to the working tree it was committed from. Part cards
# (crates/*/part.json) hold the SHA-256 of each source file, the engine reference recordings in
# tests/engine-reference/ are compared byte for byte, and MANIFEST.sha256 files list raw hashes.
# Any line-ending conversion on commit or checkout would change those bytes and break
# `check cards`, the fingerprint and the parity self-tests.
#
# The tree today has LF and CRLF files side by side (including Rust sources and reference inputs
# that contain CRLF bytes on purpose), so a normalising rule such as `text=auto eol=lf` would
# rewrite some of them. No conversion is the only rule that keeps every file as it is.

# No conversion for any file. This also overrides `core.autocrlf=true` set on this machine.
* -text

# Binary: never converted, never diffed or merged as text.
# Engine reference recordings (tokenizer bytes, token ids, tensors). Some `.u8` files are
# decoded text with CRLF bytes; they must stay exactly as recorded.
*.u8 binary
*.i32 binary
*.f16 binary
*.f32 binary
*.bin binary
# Prebuilt GPU kernels, embedded into nmffi at build time.
*.fatbin binary
# Model weights and muscle memory packs (normally outside git; listed so they are never converted).
*.safetensors binary
*.nmmusc binary
# Images and fonts used by the interface.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
